Usage: nimbu channels delete --channel=STRING

Delete a channel (requires --force)

Flags:
      --channel=STRING            Channel ID or slug

Safety:
      --force                     Skip confirmations for destructive operations
  -y, --yes                       Same as --force; also confirms protected
                                  environments

Global Flags:
  -h, --help                      Show context-sensitive help.
      --env=STRING                Named project environment (overrides site and
                                  API URL)
      --site=STRING               Site ID/subdomain (else nimbu.yml, config)
                                  ($NIMBU_SITE)
      --json                      Output JSON to stdout ($NIMBU_JSON)
      --plain                     Output stable TSV to stdout ($NIMBU_PLAIN)
      --verbose                   Enable verbose logging
      --debug                     Enable debug logging (HTTP traces)
      --version                   Print version and exit

Output:
      --color="auto"              Color output: auto|always|never ($NIMBU_COLOR)
      --no-progress               Disable live progress UI ($NIMBU_NO_PROGRESS)

Agent/CI:
      --no-input                  Never prompt; fail instead (for CI)
                                  ($NIMBU_NO_INPUT)
      --readonly                  Disable all write operations ($NIMBU_READONLY)
      --enable-commands=STRING    Comma-separated allowlist of commands
                                  ($NIMBU_ENABLE_COMMANDS)

Connection:
      --apiurl="https://api.nimbu.io"
                                  API base URL ($NIMBU_API_URL)
      --timeout=30s               Request timeout ($NIMBU_TIMEOUT)
